cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these conjectures or this code, please cite it as below."
title: "gpu-pcf-conjectures: three continued fractions found by GPU search (one conjecture, two cases of a proved family)"
authors:
  - family-names: "El Hmissi"
    given-names: "Maher"
version: "1.1.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24485588"
date-released: "2026-11-28"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Maher75017/gpu-pcf-conjectures"
abstract: "Three polynomial continued fractions found by a GPU search, matching 1/(pi-3), 2/ln(27/16) and 3/ln(1024/729) to about 220 digits. Version 1.1.0: the last two are proved. They are the cases k = 2, 3 of an infinite family given by Euler's continued fraction of the series sum 1/(m(2m-1)k^(2m-1)), with value k/((k-1)ln(k-1)+(k+1)ln(k+1)-2k ln k). The first, for 1/(pi-3), remains a numerical conjecture and does not have this structure. Includes the search code, positive and negative controls, negative results and corrections."
keywords:
  - continued fractions
  - experimental mathematics
  - Ramanujan Machine
  - conjectures
  - GPU
